esentative Matt Van Epps, a Republican incumbent in a district that leans Republican by about eleven points, faces Democrat Darden Copeland, a Nashville businessman who won his primary in August. Van Epps has raised roughly $2.3 million and benefits from about $2.5 million in outside support, though Democrats have also spent heavily against him. Copeland has raised under $900,000 and trails in cash on hand. Two minor independent candidates are also on the ballot.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the seat Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Copeland only about a 3% chance. The race has drawn attention from an ethics complaint Copeland filed accusing Van Epps of misusing tax dollars, and President Trump is expected to hold a rally in the district in early October. The fundamentals and outside assessments all point to a Republican hold, with the main question being the size of the margin rather than the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0399, "margin": -11.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0635, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0506, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0318, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0486, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0413, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0174, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0197, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0585, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0233, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0193, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0334, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0457, "margin": -11.5}]}